# Line endings are content here, not formatting.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# For most files that is invisible, but this repository hashes some of its own
# bytes, and a rewritten byte is a different hash:
#
#   * contracts/ carries the vendored Synapse contract schema and fixtures,
#     whose sha256 must match contracts/PARITY.json byte-for-byte in BOTH this
#     repo and subjective-retrieval (CLAUDE.md rule 9). On a Windows checkout
#     the schema hashed 856ccba6... instead of 3a7a8a06... and
#     tests/test_contract_parity.py failed for every Windows contributor while
#     passing in CI — a false failure that is easy to dismiss as flakiness and
#     dangerous to dismiss, because a *real* parity break looks identical.
#   * tests/fixtures/ content is hashed by the idempotency suite for the same
#     reason: re-indexing unchanged bytes must produce an unchanged state.
#
# Default everything text to LF so a checkout is byte-identical on every
# platform, then pin the hashed paths explicitly so the intent survives
# someone changing the default later.
* text=auto eol=lf

contracts/** text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.m4a binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.zst binary
*.pyc binary

# Windows-only scripts that must keep CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
